WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:06.090
In 2022, 149 million children
under five were stunted.

2
00:00:06.140 --> 00:00:10.290
The same year, 2.5 billion
adults were overweight,

3
00:00:10.340 --> 00:00:13.810
890 million of them living with obesity.

4
00:00:13.860 --> 00:00:20.990
Between 2012 and 2024, child stunting
fell while adult obesity rose from 12.1

5
00:00:21.040 --> 00:00:23.150
to 16.2 per cent.

6
00:00:23.200 --> 00:00:27.230
Too little food and
too much, in one world.

7
00:00:27.280 --> 00:00:28.070
How?

8
00:00:28.120 --> 00:00:31.190
Is it just rich countries
against poor ones?

9
00:00:31.240 --> 00:00:35.250
In this mission, you'll follow
Barry Popkin's nutrition transition:

10
00:00:35.300 --> 00:00:38.990
how diets and activity
shift as societies change.

11
00:00:39.040 --> 00:00:43.430
Then you'll weigh the physical and
human processes behind what people eat,

12
00:00:43.480 --> 00:00:47.010
from climate and soils
to floods in Bangladesh.

13
00:00:47.060 --> 00:00:50.870
Your mission: explain how the
world, and even one country,

14
00:00:50.920 --> 00:00:54.200
can have too little food
and too much at once.
